<title>AUSTRALIA: BHP says 10-month gas output down six pct.</title>
<headline>BHP says 10-month gas output down six pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Thursday gas production for the 10 months to end-March was down six percent to 207 billion cubic feet on the previous corresponding period, while production of oil and condensate was up two percent to 57.292 million barrels.  </p>
<p>BHP said oil and condensate production was up one percent for March, with higher Bass Strait production reflecting the contribution from Bream B, West Tuna and the Cobia infill drilling programmes.</p>
<p>Other Australian oil and condensate production was lower for March than for the same period last year. This was partly due to the abandonment of the Skua field in the Timor Sea after it reached the end of its commercial life and lower production at Griffin offshore Western Australia, BHP said.</p>
<p>Gas production declined for March, down eight percent, and for the year to date due to the divestment of assets, it said.  </p>
